{"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events"},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The types every other module shares: the "},{"code":"Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" protocol, the values its properties can hold, and the record a tracker makes of each event."}],"metadata":{"externalID":"Events","modules":[{"name":"Events"}],"role":"collection","roleHeading":"Framework","title":"Events","symbolKind":"module"},"topicSections":[{"title":"Events","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Event","doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/ConsentCategory","doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/EventSchema"],"anchor":"Events"},{"title":"Property values","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Sensitive","doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Refined","doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Refinement","doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Constraint","doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/ValidationKeyword","doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/UnsatisfiedConstraint","doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/ConstraintViolation"],"anchor":"Property-values"},{"title":"Records","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/EventRecord","doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/SourceLocation"],"anchor":"Records"},{"title":"Stores","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/DeliveryTag","doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Acknowledger"],"anchor":"Stores"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/events"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"An event is a value that conforms to ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Event","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":", declared with ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Its stored properties","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are its properties, so a misspelled or mistyped one is a compile error. Its type gives the name","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"destinations record it under, the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/ConsentCategory","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" whose consent decides whether it is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"delivered, and the version of its shape. Each has a default: the type’s name,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/ConsentCategory\/analytics","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" and 1.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Two property types carry rules of their own. A "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Sensitive"},{"type":"text","text":" value, such as an email address,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"prints as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<redacted>"},{"type":"text","text":" and has no public accessor: a destination reads it through"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/EventRecord\/reveal(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", which gives "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" once a delivery has redacted the record. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Refined"},{"type":"text","text":" value satisfies every "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Constraint"},{"type":"text","text":" its "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Refinement"},{"type":"text","text":" lists, checked once as it is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"made: the plain initializer traps on a value that breaks one, and "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Refined\/init(checked:)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"throws "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/UnsatisfiedConstraint"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A tracker (module "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Trackers"},{"type":"text","text":") makes an "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/EventRecord","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" of each event it tracks: the event, its own"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"random identifier, when and where it was tracked, and the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ServiceContext"},{"type":"text","text":" it was tracked in."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Destinations receive batches of these records."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Declare an event with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Event"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventMacros"},{"type":"text","text":", part of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"import Traffluent"},{"type":"text","text":"). It derives"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Event"},{"type":"text","text":" conformance from the struct’s declaration and fills in its "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/EventSchema"},{"type":"text","text":", and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Constrained"},{"type":"text","text":" beside a property fills in "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Event\/constraintViolation()"},{"type":"text","text":". To write the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"conformance by hand instead, see "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Event"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["import Traffluent","","enum PlanName: Refinement {","    static let constraints: [Constraint<String>] = [.minLength(1), .maxLength(32)]","}","","@Event(consent: .functional)","struct SignedUp {","    var plan: Refined<String, PlanName>","    var email: Sensitive<String>","}","","let event = SignedUp(plan: Refined(\"pro\"), email: Sensitive(\"ada@example.com\"))","let record = EventRecord(event: event, timestamp: .now, sourceLocation: nil)","let name = record.name  \/\/ \"SignedUp\"","let email = record.reveal(event.email)  \/\/ nil: a record made by hand keeps its sensitive values redacted","let empty = try? Refined<String, PlanName>(checked: \"\")  \/\/ nil: it throws UnsatisfiedConstraint.minLength"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The umbrella guide on this area is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/definingevents"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"references":{"doc://Events/documentation/Events/EventRecord":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/EventRecord","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A tracked event: the event itself, when it was tracked, where, and the context it was tracked in."}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EventRecord","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EventRecord","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/events\/eventrecord","title":"EventRecord","role":"symbol"},"doc://Events/documentation/Events/EventRecord/revealsSensitive